{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix pushed as Gerrit change 1641 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1641).\n\nShape of the change:\n- NEW src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/impossible_links.py — classify() maps a link failure to closed_source / redundant_ancestry / cycle, or to None. None is the safety valve: an unrecognised failure is never recorded and keeps today's retry-next-pass behaviour, so a transient fault cannot be misfiled as permanent. ImpossibleLinkStore persists verdicts to .bridge_state/impossible_links.json (a SEPARATE file from bindings.json, so it cannot collide with the peer-confirmation record epic despotic-floriated-leopard plans there).\n- The invalidation key is a \"deciding digest\": a hash over exactly the inputs the three validators read — each endpoint's status, parent chain, and dep set. Reopen the closed source or reparent an endpoint and the digest stops matching, so the link is re-attempted once, unassisted. A comment on an endpoint does NOT invalidate it (tested), or the churn would return by the back door on an active store.\n- apply_inbound_records._inbound_update_apply_links: ADD branch only — consult the record before spending the write, classify+record after a failure. The REMOVE branch and _inbound_unlink_one are untouched.\n- Logging: a newly-recorded impossible link still WARNs once (a genuinely new one stays loud); repeat skips become one INFO summary per pass naming the store path. The permanent WARNING floor drains without anything being hidden.\n\nOverlap check vs despotic-floriated-leopard: NO conflict. That epic owns the inbound REMOVAL path (_inbound_unlink_one, differ G3/G4/G5) and a peer-confirmation record in the binding store; this owns the inbound ADD path and a distinct state file. The two are complementary and neither reads the other's record.\n\nVerification: the headline test counts rebar.link invocations across two passes against a REAL store (pass 1 = 1 attempt, pass 2 = 0), deliberately not asserting on log text, since a log-shaped assertion would also pass for mere suppression. RED was confirmed by temporarily disabling the skip: 3 behavioural cells fail without it. 14 new tests pass; 2397 reconciler tests green; make lint and make typecheck exit 0."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786518157776248001,"uuid":"4c8948b3-0e8c-4404-b07f-7b0641025bc3"}